  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.8.0: Prepared asset interpolation support and version alignment\n- Released alongside JRK.JevRunner and JRK.JevRunner.Image with the shared package version.\n- JEV100 now detects AssetAndStateReference interpolations that lose automatic backtick quoting when converted to plain strings. The existing code fix wraps the interpolation in Escape.Interpolated.\n- JEV101 now detects redundant explicit backticks around AssetAndStateReference arguments in preserved interpolations. The existing code fix removes only the adjacent backticks.\n- Both rules recognize derived asset records and transitive generic constraints, matching the runtime formatter's use of the asset's StateReference.\n- Automatically installed through the JRK.JevRunner package dependency.",
